spec gg04-label-churn-at-pinned-snapshot-lpg: 2 sessions, 10 permutations
# GG04. s0 pins a read snapshot and counts :L twice — the label store (seek) beside a
# label test over every node (scan); s1 adds :L to u and removes it from l0 in two
# autocommit statements. The pinned reader's count is unchanged (10) and seek = scan.
# Through the lpg API: Graph.BeginRead, SetNodeLabel, RemoveNodeLabel.
# The final dangling probe must count 0 in every permutation: an edge to a dead node
# is never committed (catalogue §9 point 3).

starting permutation: s0c1 s0c2 s0c s1a s1r
step s0c1: lpg: live nodes labelled L at the pinned snapshot
labelled
--------
10      
(1 row)
step s0c2: lpg: live nodes labelled L at the pinned snapshot
labelled
--------
10      
(1 row)
step s0c: lpg: Graph.EndRead
step s1a: lpg: SetNodeLabel(u, L)
step s1r: lpg: RemoveNodeLabel(l0, L)
final count: MATCH (n:L) WITH count(n) AS seek OPTIONAL MATCH (m) WHERE 'L' IN labels(m) RETURN seek, count(m) AS scan
seek|scan
----+----
10  |10  
(1 row)
final final: MATCH (n) RETURN n.name AS name ORDER BY name
name
